.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Parquet caches are large and refetchable, so data/ is ignored by default.
# Two subdirectories must ship: the agent's committed state and journal, and the
# CBOE benchmark CSVs a judge needs to reproduce the report offline.
# This has to be `data/*` and not `data/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so a negation inside one never fires.
data/*
!data/state/
!data/benchmarks/
# The implied-volatility record accumulates one observation a day and takes a
# year to rebuild. Ignoring it would mean the scheduled runner starts from an
# empty history every run and iv_rank never becomes a number.
!data/iv_history/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.remember/
graphify-out/
# The working SQLite store is one run's scratch space. The durable copy is the
# committed snapshot at data/state/wheels.json — see store.py for why both exist.
*.db
